  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging is expected to take hold across the Northern Rockies\nand extending into the Northern High Plains this weekend into\nearly next week. This will lead to dry weather conditions from\nlarge scale subsidence along with warmer temperatures. NBM mean is\nnow showing widespread temperatures into the 70s on Monday and 70s\nand 80s on Tuesday.\n\nEnsembles show the ridge axis sliding downstream of the region \nwith the next trough becoming established over the western U.S.\nstarting Tuesday night or Wednesday. This pattern will send \ndiffluent southwest upper flow into eastern Montana with ample \nPacific moisture. The trough and low pressure system will \ngradually track east, maintaining rain chances at times for the \nsecond half of next week along with markedly cooler temperatures.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was largely followed over the next several days given upper\nlevel ridging and relatively dry weather conditions. Confidence is\nhigh on the warm and dry conditions through Tuesday before the\ntrough comes in with falling temperatures and increasing rain\nchances for the second half of next week. While QPF amounts have\ntrended down this cycle, widespread QPF ranging from 0.25\" and\n0.75\" are within the most likely ensemble envelope during this\nperiod. Thus, confidence is high on a shifting pattern toward\ncooler and wetter weather, but more modest on specific amounts.",
